      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To add to this:\nCustom Emote Animations in SDK3 that change transforms (such as dances) work perfectly fine locally, but when viewed on a remote client (other users), they do not change the Root Transform of the animation on any axis where they would normally work with a SDK2 avatar. \nWhen an avatar's scale is not set to 1, this places the avatars into the ground or air and do not move side to side.\nHowever when Safety Settings > Custom Animations are disabled, the remote viewer can see these Custom Emote Animations perfectly fine, but then can no longer view other animations such as material changes or showing objects.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
